  "prompt": "Which expression is equivalent to $x^{4}-16$?",
  "choices": {
    "A": "$(x-4)(x+4)(x^{2}+1)$",
    "B": "$(x^{2}-4)(x+4)$",
    "C": "$(x-2)(x+2)(x^{2}+4)$",
    "D": "$(x^{2}-4)(x^{2}-4)$"
  },
  "correctAnswer": "C",
  "explanation": "The expression $x^4-16$ can be rewritten as $(x^2)^2-4^2$. Using the difference of squares formula $a^2-b^2=(a-b)(a+b)$, this gives $(x^2-4)(x^2+4)$. The factor $x^2-4$ is also a difference of squares: $x^2-4=(x-2)(x+2)$. Therefore, $x^4-16=(x-2)(x+2)(x^2+4)$.",
